adf5e-23a4-4fa2-b812-e7ddd81dcf78","position":{"commit_sha":"4977c4e6243837f6eadb5641b37fc053ad5d7d70","position":"1789023256252231001-fadadf5e-23a4-4fa2-b812-e7ddd81dcf78"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA/fix: _check_home_escape treated any argv Name/Attribute called home, mkdtemp, or TemporaryDirectory as a home escape, so unrelated locals and tmp_path-rooted temp helpers could false-positive. Fixed in Gerrit 2953 by detecting only concrete Path.home() and os.environ['HOME']/imported environ['HOME'] AST forms. Also replaced the conftest source-grep UsageError check with behavioral assertion and pinned module-level helper opt-out fallback. RED evidence: new focused guard tests failed before the implementation. Verification: tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py passed; full make verify passed with PYTEST_WORKERS=2 and GIT_CONFIG_* unset; Gerrit 2953 passed LLM-Review+1 and Verified+1 and is merged.","timestamp":1789019524768667001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Merged Gerrit 2953 and attempted normal completion close, but verify_completion gate admission is currently congested (all 2 host slots in use). No verdict was produced. Waiting and retrying without force.","timestamp":1789021077935002001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788330600560697001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"56495192-45dd-46dc-bceb-ffaf2f14d0ff","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"15f2-f3d4-ffcd-4223"},{"link_uuid":"9220eaba-5363-42c6-ae86-96a8beea991d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"827d-6ebb-901b-4530"},{"link_uuid":"7ca27211-4f23-42a1-8945-29af2f3501b9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8493-6c74-9ca6-4ead"},{"link_uuid":"6a751945-d516-477f-b714-3fe26c6b96c7","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8189-c171-e4b7-4389"}],"description":"## Context\nThree follow-ups on the unit-tier subprocess-isolation guard, all raised as non-blocking advisories by the LLM code review on Gerrit 2506 and deferred there.\n\n`tests/_subprocess_isolation.py` protects the unit suite from subprocesses that escape the per-test sandbox. The current `_check_home_escape` rule can over-flag any argv expression that merely references a name or attribute called `home`, `mkdtemp`, or `TemporaryDirectory`, even when the value is an unrelated local or an already-harnessed `tmp_path` value. False positives are costly because they redden innocent files and encourage reverting the guard.\n\nTwo guard contracts are also under-tested: the collection-time violation must raise `pytest.UsageError` (not `pytest.fail`, which appears as an xdist INTERNALERROR), and hazards found in module-level helper functions must honor the file-level/module `pytestmark` opt-out fallback when no individual test name is available.\n\n## Outcome\nNarrow home-escape detection to concrete escape forms that actually leave the harness, while preserving true positives for `Path.home()` and `os.environ[\"HOME\"]`. Add behavioral regression tests for the narrowed negative/positive cases, the `UsageError` contract, and module-level-helper file-level opt-out behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `_check_home_escape` reports real home escapes such as `Path.home()` and `os.environ[\"HOME\"]` but does not report unrelated locals named `home`, `mkdtemp`, or `TemporaryDirectory`, nor harnessed `tmp_path`-rooted mkdtemp usage.\n- [x] A behavioral unit test asserts collection-time isolation violations raise `pytest.UsageError` instead of source-grepping for the error text.\n- [x] A behavioral unit test proves a module-level helper hazard is covered by a file-level/module `pytestmark` opt-out fallback when the finding has no specific test name.\n\n## Testing\n- RED: run targeted tests in `tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py` and confirm the new contracts fail on unmodified `origin/main`.\n- GREEN: rerun the targeted guard tests after the implementation change.\n- Verification: run `make verify PYTEST_WORKERS=2` with inherited `GIT_CONFIG_*` variables unset before pushing.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/_subprocess_isolation.py","reason":"narrow home-escape detection and preserve guard behavior"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_collection_isolation_guard.py","reason":"pin narrowed home-escape, UsageError, and module-level opt-out contracts"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","8189-c171-e4b7-4389"],["relates_to","827d-6ebb-901b-4530"],["relates_to","8493-6c74-9ca6-4ead"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"7d4b3e54-6d49-4cd2-a87f-bb4518950a79","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"c678-e73c-b48a-4bbe","ticket_type":"task","title":"Narrow the isolation guard's home-escape rule and pin two untested contracts","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["caf2c058-a5fc-47d6-a54c-29f4477ccac7","4d190044-ae4f-4d95-922d-fed4508cbd65","ff6353c9-44f2-4271-95ce-a8141fb8996e","595ff9d6-1a86-441d-97c6-6c959ee88f01","483a8fd9-c21b-4aaa-b3e3-d7f478fbc3b0","9220eaba-5363-42c6-ae86-96a8beea991d","7ca27211-4f23-42a1-8945-29af2f3501b9","fc6de452-72ca-40db-a5b4-c8718b70ba80","2c905406-07cc-4c76-9c81-8501ec204484","6a751945-d516-477f-b714-3fe26c6b96c7","1d750891-e8a2-4fe3-b318-6b38fdf608a9","7d4b3e54-6d49-4cd2-a87f-bb4518950a79","fadadf5e-23a4-4fa2-b812-e7ddd81dcf78"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1789028933470478001,"uuid":"a6bdd36e-a978-45a8-a8b2-1523e0e6c25b"}